# x6_embed_stream: embedding table never whole on the heap. On x4's peak and x5's null.
#
#   356,302,848 B  n=2   unowned torch.int64 (28996, 768)   table as shares, twice
#    90,660,864 B  n=5   graph_param                        float32 originals
#
# basis      x5_graph_clear +0.10% at 0.03% spread (third null): at the peak the embedding is in use,
#            so no lifetime lever reaches it.
# lever      rows read from encrypt_spill_cpu's file (contiguous row range of a (V, D) int64 dump: one
#            np.fromfile with offset); materialised copy emptied before the first chunk.
# conflicts  supersedes embed_chunk_cpu (both replace Embedding.forward). Requires encrypt_spill_cpu
#            (checked at import). Weight matched by shape; refuses unless exactly one record matches.
# donor      SHAFT-GPU embed_chunk_gpu (SHAFT_EMBED_STREAM).
# free       same bytes, file and order; sixteen mask draws unchanged; gate identical to x4's expected.
# expected   up to -356 MB, 750 to 870 MB (-20% to -30%); x4 spread 0.03%. Retired endpoint 643,784 kB.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_stream_cpu.py
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_stream_cpu
